 0<=r<=lambda.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"On the R-basis a e_0,...,a e_lambda established above, x(ae_i)=(lambda-i+1)ae_(i-1), y(ae_i)=(i+1)ae_(i+1), and h(ae_i)=(lambda-2i)ae_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Let F_p be the prime subfield of K, canonically isomorphic to R/pR=Z/pZ. The images of a e_i form an F_p-basis of M_R/pM_R because they are an R-basis of M_R. The natural map M_R/pM_R -> M tensor_Z F_p is an isomorphism: for a Z-basis of M, localization at integers prime to p reduces to the same F_p-basis. Extending scalars F_p -> K gives the K-basis b_0,...,b_lambda of M tensor_Z K, where b_i denotes the image of a e_i under these quotient and scalar-extension maps. These maps carry each integral action matrix to its reduction and then to K, so x b_i=(lambda-i+1)b_(i-1), y b_i=(i+1)b_(i+1), h b_i=(lambda-2i)b_i, with out-of-range terms zero. Thus this explicitly identifies the reduced representation and action; the characteristic-zero e_i are not vectors of M tensor_Z K.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/3/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"a\\\",\\\"e_i\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"h\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"M_R\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"M\\\",\\\"L(K)\\\",\\\"b_i\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/text\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"For 0<=r<=lambda<p, r! is invertible modulo p, so the reductions of X_r and Y_r are scalar multiples of the corresponding powers of x and y on M tensor_Z K. The characteristic-zero identities defining E_i,j preserve M_R and their matrices in the R-basis a e_t are the usual matrix-unit matrices. Reduction modulo p and extension to K therefore give the matrix units in the explicitly defined basis b_0,...,b_lambda; equivalently the identities from S002 persist under these maps. Every binom(lambda,j) is nonzero modulo p because 0<=j<=lambda<p, hence is a unit in F_p and K. Thus any K-subspace W invariant under x and y is invariant under each reduced E_i,j. Write a nonzero w in W as w=sum_i c_i b_i and choose i with c_i nonzero. For every j, the reduced E_j,i sends w to c_i b_j, so b_j belongs to W because c_i is invertible in K. Hence W is the whole module. The basis has lambda+1 vectors, a positive integer, so the module is nonzero. This proves irreducibility, including lambda=0 and p=2.\\\"},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"replace\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/argument/4/objects\\\",\\\"value\\\":[\\\"r\\\",\\\"lambda\\\",\\\"p\\\",\\\"X_r\\\",\\\"Y_r\\\",\\\"x\\\",\\\"y\\\",\\\"E_i,j\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"W\\\",\\\"b_i\\\"]},{\\\"op\\\":\\\"add\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/graph/inferences/0/locals/-\\\",\\\"value\\\":{\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"F_p\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"prime subfield of K, canonically R/pR\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"start\\\":\\\"S004\\\",\\\"end\\\":\\\"S005\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"definition\\\",\\\"declaration\\\":\\\"Let F_p be the prime subfield of K, canonically isomorphic to R/pR=Z/pZ.\\\",\\\"from_inputs\\\":[\\\"H001\\\",\\\"H002\\\"],\\\"from_local\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"p\\\",\\\"K\\\",\\\"R\\\"]}}]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Stop this stage honestly on a substantive or suspected proof gap, unavailable source, or input conflict. JSON fields: status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. Status must be SUBSTANTIVE_GAP, SUSPECTED_GAP, SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT. Difficulty alone is not a mathematical error.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parame